            <h4>REET &amp; Education Department Teachers</h4>
            <div class="cadre-badge">Primary, Secondary &amp; Senior Secondary</div>
            <p><strong>Covered Ranks:</strong> Grade-III Teachers (Level L-10: ₹33,800), Grade-II Senior Teachers (Level L-11: ₹37,800), and Grade-I School Lecturers (Level L-12: ₹44,300).</p>
            <p><strong>Impact:</strong> Teachers represent the single largest cadre in the state. Under the 8th CPC, entry basic pay for Grade-III teachers will rise from ₹33,800 to <strong>₹77,064 per month</strong> upon confirmation.</p>
            <span class="cadre-footer">Grade-III (7th CPC): ₹33,800 | 8th CPC (2.28x): <strong>₹77,064</strong></span>
          </div>

          <div class="cadre-box police">
            <h4>Rajasthan Police Department</h4>
            <div class="cadre-badge">Law Enforcement &amp; RAC Battalions</div>
            <p><strong>Covered Ranks:</strong> Constables (Level L-4: ₹20,800), Head Constables (Level L-8: ₹24,700), Assistant Sub-Inspectors (Level L-9: ₹29,200), and Sub-Inspectors (Level L-10: ₹33,800).</p>
            <p><strong>Impact:</strong> Constables will see their confirmed starting basic pay jump to <strong>₹47,424</strong>, alongside dedicated uniform and mess allowance increments.</p>
            <span class="cadre-footer">Constable (7th CPC): ₹20,800 | 8th CPC (2.28x): <strong>₹47,424</strong></span>
          </div>

