      </section>

      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>House Rent Allowance (HRA) Classification Across Rajasthan</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike three-tier central models, House Rent Allowance in Rajasthan is categorized into <strong>two distinct geographic classifications</strong> under the Rajasthan Civil Services (HRA) Rules:
        </p>

        <div class="city-classification-grid">
          <div class="city-box tier-y">
            <h4>Class Y Cities (Urban Centers)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Five Major Corporation Cities</div>
            <p><strong>Projected HRA Rate:</strong> 18% of Basic Pay (or enhanced ceiling rate).</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Cities:</strong> Jaipur, Jodhpur, Kota, Ajmer, and Bikaner.</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Reflects prominent commercial, educational, and divisional hubs.</span>
          </div>

